*> Acceptance test of docs/protocol/15a-brigadier-command-library.md §11 Comparison with 15-commands-framework.md: every row marked
*> C (confirmed) or D (differs) is a statement about the parser that a case checks, in the form the framework implements (a D row
*> means 15 was wrong and the library reading, 15a, holds). The tree is that of the §8 test plus adm (a command that needs level
*> 2), run (a redirect to the root) and nc (no command; child x). A leading 0> parses as a source of level 0; a leading S<level>>
*> lists the suggestions at the end of the line (sug=). Rows marked N (game side, or not readable from the library) have no case.

